# Thornvault Forager with Corpseberry Cultivator: foraging to pay the Forager's mana ability is a forage (CR 701.61a), so "whenever you
# forage" triggers; that trigger does not trigger from the mana ability's activation and adds no mana, so it is no mana ability
# (CR 605.1b) and is put on the stack the next time a player would receive priority (CR 117.3, 603.3). Turn 1: Black Lotus pays for the
# Cultivator, the Forest and a Mox Emerald for the Forager, the other Mox for Gilded Goose and its Food. Turn 3: the Forager forages by
# sacrificing the Food for {G}{G}; the Cultivator's trigger waits on the stack and its counter comes when it resolves.

[Bot1 Deck]
Thornvault Forager
Forest
Mox Emerald
Mox Emerald
Black Lotus
Gilded Goose
Corpseberry Cultivator
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Hand.Corpseberry Cultivator.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Thornvault Forager.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Gilded Goose.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Food Token.Subtypes = Food
Bot1.Decline
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Thornvault Forager.Activate(Ability: Forage)
Bot1.Colors(Green; Green)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Food Token = (absent)
? Stack.Count = 1
? Bot1.Battlefield.Corpseberry Cultivator.Power = 2
? Bot1.Mana = {G}{G}
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Stack.Count = 0
? Bot1.Battlefield.Corpseberry Cultivator.Power = 3

[Expect]
Bot1.Mana = {G}{G}
Bot1.Battlefield.Corpseberry Cultivator.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
